WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.070
Hello and welcome to your second drink of The Surplus.

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:11.110
This is the episode where Oscar explains to Michael that he has to spend the office surplus

3
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.430
and it kicks off this big debate over what the bullpen wants to spend it on,

4
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.010
chairs or a new copier.

5
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.410
This is also when Dwight takes Angela and Andy to Shroot FarMs.

6
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.670
It was a very fun episode of The Office, one of my favorite to shoot,

7
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.890
and also one of my favorite episodes of Office Ladies.

8
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.930
So listen, lady, I was revisiting this one and I did this deep dive on butter sculptures

9
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.830
at the Iowa State Fair because when Angela is talking about planning her wedding,

10
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.730
she says she wants a cat butter sculpture.

11
00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:41.650
Mm-hmm.

12
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:47.530
I remember when we did our stories, you sent me all of these pictures you found of butter sculptures.

13
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:47.930
Yes.

14
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.070
Well, guess what?

15
00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.330
I have an update.

16
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.390
Okay.

17
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.810
A butter sculpture update.

18
00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:59.910
I want everyone to know that the Iowa State Fair will be going on this year from August 13th to 23rd.

19
00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.910
And yes, there will be a butter cow per usual.

20
00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:10.190
And it will be sculpted by Sarah Pratt, who has been making the butter cow since 2006.

21
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.130
Her two daughters, Hannah and Grace, are now her apprentices.

22
00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:20.570
And listen, I'm telling you, I got so interested in these sculptures again that I ended up watching

23
00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:24.050
some videos of Sarah and her daughters from last year's fair.

24
00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:28.950
And they use their hands a lot to do the sculpting.

25
00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.790
I don't know what I was expecting.

26
00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:31.390
Tools?

27
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:32.230
I don't know.

28
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:38.110
I totally envision it as like them using their hands, like almost like a clay, like making pottery.

29
00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.450
That is what it was like.

30
00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:45.330
I envisioned it like, I don't know, like an old-timey like chisel and hammer.

31
00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.410
But no, they do.

32
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.130
They use their hands to mold it.

33
00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.490
And then it cools into the shape that they're going for.

34
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.170
It's really fascinating.

35
00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:53.990
I want to watch it.

36
00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.750
And one day, I need to see these butter sculptures in real life.

37
00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.350
Can we please do this, lady?

38
00:01:59.470 --> 00:01:59.950
I mean it.

39
00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.550
I mean, I am in.

40
00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.190
I love butter.

41
00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.850
I know you do.

42
00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.930
And I love things sculpted out of other things, I guess.

43
00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:13.830
This is a good match for us.

44
00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:14.650
Mm-hmm.

45
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:20.890
Well, lady, this is also the episode where we finally gave you your first work birthday.

46
00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:22.210
Yeah.

47
00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.050
But your cake was late.

48
00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.210
It was a whole thing.

49
00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.690
You can listen to it in the episode.

50
00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:32.150
But when we put a call out to our listeners to tell us their favorite moment from the surplus,

51
00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:37.410
we got this letter from Jordan G in Orlando and Angela I had to share.

52
00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.490
Jordan said,

53
00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:39.550
Hi, ladies.

54
00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:44.910
This is more of a response to your episode of the podcast and less about the show itself.

55
00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:51.270
I'm currently listening to the surplus episode for the first time where Angela gets her first work birthday party.

56
00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:56.290
I just want to say how touching that moment was when Angela was surprised with her cake.

57
00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.390
It literally made me tear up.

58
00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:04.350
One of my favorite things about the podcast is being able to have a look into the friendship between you two.

59
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:12.130
It is so honest and special, and your obvious connection and love for one another is truly something so amazing to get to witness.

60
00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:15.230
You make me laugh, cry, and everything in between.

61
00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.450
I feel like I'm right there with you.

62
00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:21.250
I'm sure you've heard it a million times, so what's one time more?

63
00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.770
Thank you for creating something so special for everyone.

64
00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.750
Many blessings to both you and your family.

65
00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.590
Love always, Jordan.

66
00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.810
Well, Jordan, gosh, that just, you know what, just completely made my day.

67
00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.210
Thank you so much.

68
00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:36.870
I know.

69
00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.470
I thought that was so sweet.

70
00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:45.070
And she also had a PS, I guess, I met Jordan in Arizona at the University of Arizona in 2018.

71
00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.650
I had done a book signing for The Actor's Life.

72
00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:53.050
She said, I was literally one of the last people in line, and you still took time to talk with me and sign my book.

73
00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.770
And as an actor who now gets paid full-time to perform.

74
00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.190
Way to go, Jordan.

75
00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:58.850
Yes.

76
00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:03.410
It was huge encouraging me through those tough times we all face.

77
00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.470
Ah, Jordan, yay!

78
00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:06.370
Congratulations.

79
00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.390
And thank you for writing in.

80
00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.950
Thank you so much, Jordan.

81
00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.150
Well, I have a letter here from Hannah B.

82
00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.850
in Canada who says,

83
00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.890
First off, love you ladies so much.

84
00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:22.030
I rewatched The Surplus recently and love the scene where Michael calls in Hank to make the final decision,

85
00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:26.470
especially the moment when Hank realizes the power he's been given.

86
00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:32.990
Was it scripted that he would take the jelly beans and Michael responds very seriously that he can take as many as he wants?

87
00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.270
Stephen Hughes' energy in this scene is hilarious.

88
00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.750
I mean, it is so fantastic.

89
00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.690
Hannah, we mentioned in our breakdown that this is our favorite as well.

90
00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:43.550
Oh, yes.

91
00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:44.390
So much.

92
00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.310
It's so good.

93
00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:52.310
And Hannah, I went to the script and it was scripted that Hank takes some jelly beans, but that's all it said.

94
00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.910
Steve improvised the line, take as many as you want.

95
00:04:55.910 --> 00:05:04.630
And Hugh improvised the thank you, thank you, before his next scripted line that was, you know, it's nice and warm up here.

96
00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:17.650
And I actually think this little bit that Hannah points out is such a great example of improv on the show, Ang, because we weren't improvising whole scenes.

97
00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:24.510
We would have a scripted bit and then we'd do some little thing and then we'd go back to scripted and we did it so seamlessly.

98
00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:31.610
Yeah, because we had really great writing when there were these little moments where we could sort of add a little color.

99
00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.150
We knew right where to do them.

100
00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:35.970
Do you know what I mean?

101
00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.170
It was just so organic.

102
00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:38.870
Yes.

103
00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:50.030
Oh, and lady, while I was poking around in the script looking for the answer to this question, oh my gosh, I found not one, but two cold opens for this episode.

104
00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.610
We did not talk about this in our breakdown.

105
00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:53.670
Ooh.

106
00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:57.350
And this episode does not have a standalone cold open.

107
00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.350
We just get right into the plot.

108
00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.370
Oscar just enters Michael's office and tells him about the surplus.

109
00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:06.930
But there were actually two standalone cold opens written for this episode.

110
00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:10.550
I think we only ended up filming one of them.

111
00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:14.230
It got added back to the top of the Peacock Superfan episode.

112
00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.650
It is a prank that Jim pulls on Dwight.

113
00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.650
Let's hear it.

114
00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.930
What is this thing you just sent me?

115
00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:22.270
Oh, it's really cool.

116
00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.390
It's a picture of the most relaxing meadow you've ever seen.

117
00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:25.350
Idiot.

118
00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.810
I know what this is.

119
00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:30.970
It's supposed to lull me into a sense of calm and then a ghoul pops up and scares me.

120
00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:31.990
Why would I do that?

121
00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.350
Dwight, of all people, I know that you're unscarable.

122
00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:35.410
Damn right I am.

123
00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.270
Oh, hello, relaxing meadow.

124
00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:42.690
I'm so relaxed and calm looking at you right now.

125
00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.470
Oh, no, a scary ghoul just popped up.

126
00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.310
I'm so scared.

127
00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:48.130
I'm so scared.

128
00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:48.430
Really?

129
00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.690
Is this the best you could, Jim?

130
00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:51.590
How are you?

131
00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:54.670
Okay.

132
00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.000
That is the best I can do.

133
00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:02.840
He got him.

134
00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.020
He got him, lady.

135
00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.540
Yeah, so what he does, because you can't see it,

136
00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:10.180
he is right over Dwight's shoulder in a scary mask.

137
00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.660
And that is what ends up scaring Dwight.

138
00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.460
So that is now at the top of this episode in the super fan.

139
00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.480
But they wrote another cold open for this episode

140
00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:22.420
where Michael and Dwight discover that it's snowing outside.

141
00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.600
And we all run outside and have a snowball fight.

142
00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:27.080
But there's not a lot of snow.

143
00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.800
So the snow is kind of like filled with pebbles.

144
00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.440
You know when you're like trying to make a snowman,

145
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.320
but there's not enough.

146
00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:34.480
Yeah.

147
00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.800
Yeah, or a snowball or whatever.

148
00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:37.700
So you get dirt and sticks and stuff.

149
00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:37.960
Yeah.

150
00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:42.160
Well, anyway, I bet they're glad they chose this one in the bullpen

151
00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.680
because then they didn't have to spend a bunch of money on fake snow

152
00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.360
just to have it get cut from the episode.

153
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.380
That's all I could think of when you shared that.

154
00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.700
I thought they were going to have to call snow business

155
00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.400
and get a bunch of fake snow.

156
00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:55.360
Yeah, but they didn't.

157
00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:56.540
I don't think we shot it.

158
00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.800
Well, I love a cold open surprise.

159
00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.840
Well, I also want to talk about this letter we got from Cassie L.

160
00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:02.880
in Milton, Florida.

161
00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.300
Cassie said,

162
00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.740
I'm currently watching the super fan episodes

163
00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.700
and there's a scene between Angela and Dwight

164
00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.460
that has been added back

165
00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:15.020
in where we find out Angela is very passionate about the Mayflower.

166
00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.080
And it seems that Dwight knows this by his reaction.

167
00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.720
So Cassie wants to know,

168
00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:23.360
how many times have they had deep conversations about the Mayflower?

169
00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.720
This scene made me laugh out loud.

170
00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.860
I went back and watched it three more times.

171
00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.080
Yeah, it was really fun.

172
00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.160
And it just, it's one of those scenes, lady,

173
00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:34.240
I loved that wasn't in the original

174
00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.660
that just shows the history of a couple.

175
00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:39.520
You know, there's all this assumed history

176
00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.620
that you carry around with you

177
00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.980
when you are in a relationship with someone

178
00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.560
and just a window into it is so delicious.

179
00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:49.720
It's like when we got to see Michael and Jan's condo,

180
00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:50.920
you know, I'm like, what?

181
00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.120
They've been living this all this time,

182
00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.500
but I thought it'd be fun to hear.

183
00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.300
It's after the scene in the kitchen

184
00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.780
where they are getting the directions to Shroot Farms,

185
00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.540
Angela and Dwight sneak out to the alleyway

186
00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.660
next to the warehouse.

187
00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:03.500
Let's listen.

188
00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:08.930
I thought you were going to put the muzzle on that singing idiot.

189
00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.750
He's not a bad singer.

190
00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.010
He is pretty talented, I guess.

191
00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:15.230
And he went to Cornell.

192
00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.610
Yeah, well, I provide America

193
00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.210
with two of its most beloved staples,

194
00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.230
beets and paper.

195
00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:23.250
His family is well-connected in pockets of Connecticut.

196
00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.130
And his ancestors came over on the Mayflower.

197
00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:26.950
Oh, big whoop.

198
00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.910
Half my family came over on a U-boat

199
00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.590
and would have destroyed the Mayflower.

200
00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:32.950
Listen to you.

201
00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:34.710
Destroyed the Mayflower?

202
00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:35.250
I'm sorry.

203
00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:36.750
I can't believe I said that.

204
00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:37.710
Angela?

205
00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:38.730
Hi.

206
00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:40.850
It's so fun.

207
00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.330
I so remember doing that scene.

208
00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:44.750
You know how some of you hear and you're like,

209
00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:45.750
I don't really remember that.

210
00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:46.530
I remember saying,

211
00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.450
deep pockets of Connecticut.

212
00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.210
It's so good.

213
00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:51.570
She's so impressed.

214
00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.230
I also love that Dwight has to admit he is a good singer.

215
00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:54.870
Mm-hmm.

216
00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:55.350
Yeah.

217
00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.490
Well, you know what's crazy

218
00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.850
is that in the background of this scene, lady,

219
00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:00.810
there's a little bit of snow on the dumpster

220
00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.250
and you guys are acting like you're really cold.

221
00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:05.150
So I kind of wonder,

222
00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.690
when did we shoot this?

223
00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:10.130
Was this before or after they decided to bail

224
00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.670
on that snow cold open?

225
00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:12.490
They were like,

226
00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:13.990
we don't know what the cold open's gonna be

227
00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:14.890
for this episode yet.

228
00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:17.730
So just throw some snow out there so it matches,

229
00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:18.690
just in case.

230
00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:19.830
Just in case.

231
00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:21.010
Okay, everyone.

232
00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:22.850
Well, thanks so much for sending in your letters

233
00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.090
about your favorite moments.

234
00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:24.990
We love them.

235
00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.170
You can submit your favorites at our website,

236
00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.330
officeladies.com.

237
00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.650
And now it's time for your second drink.

238
00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.570
Of the surplus.

239
00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:36.870
I'm Jenna Fisher.

240
00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.170
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

241
00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:39.450
We were on The Office together.

242
00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:40.690
And we're best friends.

243
00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:42.490
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office

244
00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:44.530
Rewatch podcast just for you.

245
00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:47.010
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office

246
00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:49.250
and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories

247
00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.510
that only two people who were there can tell you.

248
00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:52.630
We're The Office ladies.

249
00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.940
Today is a very special day.

250
00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:01.860
Yes.

251
00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:06.280
It is the last day that Angela will be in her 40s.

252
00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.240
It is, you guys.

253
00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.740
Guys, I am 49, staring at 50.

254
00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:13.480
By the time you guys hear this, I'll be 50.

255
00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:14.260
Yeah.

256
00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:15.300
That's crazy.

